{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMCvnztiGmXQcoG68CBx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QSqetXfzCXhRCKFFrvwNHJ","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"cases":[{"id":"inherited_session_rejection","met":true,"report_quote":"An authenticated client sends `mcp-session-id: __proto__`, `constructor` or `toString`. The lookup returns an inherited value, which is truthy, so the 404 guard is bypassed. `session.handleRequest` is then not a function, and the `async` handler throws.","reason":"Gives the plain-object sessions store, the header-controlled lookup, the non-callable handleRequest, the Express 4 async rejection, Node default termination, the bearer-secret prerequisite and line evidence. It frames the crash as inference and does not claim a tested crash. The Express and Node claims are not backed by the research packet."},{"id":"auth_boundary","met":true,"report_quote":"`app.use('/mcp', …)` covers `/mcp`, `/mcp/init` and subpaths, and it runs before all three handlers. I found no bypass in the source.","reason":"Treats the gateway auth as preceding all handlers. It makes no unauthenticated-attack claim and no OAuth audience claim."},{"id":"runtime_scope","met":true,"report_quote":"Nothing was executed or tested. Every finding comes from reading the source.","reason":"Makes no runtime, crash-measurement, deployed-secret or host-audit claims. Lists host-owned controls as unknown and needing evidence."},{"id":"coverage_get","met":true,"report_quote":"| `GET /mcp` | Session lookup, error handling | Assessed; finding 1 |","reason":"Assesses the GET lookup and the unhandled async rejection path in finding 1, with line references."},{"id":"coverage_delete","met":true,"report_quote":"| `DELETE /mcp` | Session lookup, cleanup | Assessed; findings 1 and 2 |","reason":"Assesses DELETE separately. Finding 1 cites `:22` for the lookup and `:24` for the handler. Finding 2 covers the missing cleanup.